{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneModularTwist"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting.six_strand_spin_twist_split_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting.six_strand_spin_twist_split_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwistedChannelSplitting.lean#L185-L203","doc":"The six-strand spin-only split vanishes (non-zero traces, `q ≠ 0`) iff `q² = 1`: it is a pure\n`q`-deformation effect, absent at `q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting.six_strand_spin_twist_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting.six_strand_spin_twist_split","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwistedChannelSplitting.lean#L173-L183","doc":"**Six-strand spin-only ribbon twist.**  If the ribbon twist `θ_λ = q^{c(λ)}` acts on the spin\nfactor only, the deuteron minus the singlet is `(q⁵ − q³)·tr p·tr p'`, where `p`, `p'` are the\n`(4,2)` and `(3,3)` blocks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting.theta_four_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting.theta_four_two","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwistedChannelSplitting.lean#L166-L171","doc":"At six strands the deuteron's spin shape is twisted by `q²` relative to the singlet's. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting.theta_pair_pow_four_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting.theta_pair_pow_four_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwistedChannelSplitting.lean#L151-L164","doc":"**Twist ratio between two shapes of the same size depends only on the spins.**\nFor `a + b = a' + b'`, `θ_{(a,b)}⁴ = θ_{(a',b')}⁴ · q^{(a−b)(a−b+2) − (a'−b')(a'−b'+2)}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting.contentSum_three_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting.contentSum_three_three","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwistedChannelSplitting.lean#L144-L147","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting.contentSum_four_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting.contentSum_four_two","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwistedChannelSplitting.lean#L139-L142","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting.four_mul_contentSum_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting.four_mul_contentSum_pair","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwistedChannelSplitting.lean#L131-L137","doc":"**The two-row twist exponent is a Casimir plus a size constant.**\n`4 c(a, b) = (a − b)(a − b + 2) + (a + b)(a + b − 4)`; with `2S = a − b`, `n = a + b`, this is\n`c = S(S+1) + n(n−4)/4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting.two_mul_contentSum_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting.two_mul_contentSum_pair","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwistedChannelSplitting.lean#L120-L129","doc":"**Two-row content sum.**  `2 c(a, b) = a(a−1) + b(b−3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting.two_mul_sum_range_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting.two_mul_sum_range_sub","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwistedChannelSplitting.lean#L110-L118","doc":"`2 · Σ_{j<m} (j − i) = m(m−1) − 2 i m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting.spin_only_twist_split_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting.spin_only_twist_split_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwistedChannelSplitting.lean#L92-L104","doc":"Over a domain with non-zero block traces, a spin-only twist splits the channels exactly when\nits two eigenvalues differ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting.spin_only_twist_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting.spin_only_twist_split","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwistedChannelSplitting.lean#L85-L90","doc":"**Spin-only twist.**  With the isospin factor untwisted, the split is `(s − s')·tr p·tr p'`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting.symmetric_twist_no_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting.symmetric_twist_no_split","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwistedChannelSplitting.lean#L77-L83","doc":"**A twist acting the same way on both factors cannot split the channels.**  This is the\nPauli lock of bean `qou-7zob` surviving any twist that does not distinguish spin from isospin. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting.twisted_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting.twisted_split","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwistedChannelSplitting.lean#L66-L75","doc":"**Twisted channel split.**  With twists acting by scalars on the two blocks, the deuteron\nminus the singlet is the 2×2 determinant of the twist eigenvalues times the two block traces. ","signatureChunk":0}]}